Defender-Centric Kill Chain Disruption Points
For this specific CVE, the most effective interruptions are:
Reconnaissance Phase
Reduce SharePoint internet exposure.
Limit version disclosure.
Delivery Phase
Enforce MFA.
Restrict access by IP/network segmentation.
Exploitation Phase
Upgrade to the fixed versions: 
SharePoint 2016 ≥ 16.0.5565.1001
SharePoint 2019 ≥ 16.0.10417.20198
SharePoint Subscription Edition ≥ 16.0.19725.20522 [NVD-CVE-2026-65660]
Installation/C2 Phase
Monitor IIS logs.
Detect unexpected PowerShell activity.
Hunt for newly created ASPX files and web shells.
Actions on Objectives Phase
Use EDR detection.
Monitor SharePoint service accounts.
Alert on unusual document repository access patterns.
From a kill chain viewpoint, CVE-2026-65660 is most critical because it provides a reliable bridge between the Exploitation and Installation phases. Once code execution is achieved on a SharePoint server, the server often becomes a launch pad for broader enterprise compromise, making rapid patching and post-patching threat hunting essential. 

